[agent:result] === fg append-features ===
[agent:result] Usage: hops fg append-features [OPTIONS] NAME
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Append new columns to an existing feature group, in place.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Append-only schema evolution: it keeps the same feature group version so
[agent:result]   downstream consumers are never disturbed. Existing columns cannot be
[agent:result]   dropped, renamed, or retyped from here; that is a breaking change, so bump
[agent:result]   to a new version instead. New columns cannot be primary or partition keys,
[agent:result]   and existing rows are not backfilled (they read null until reinserted).
[agent:result]   Feature views built on this feature group keep their old projection and do
[agent:result]   not see the appended columns; create a new feature view to use them.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Args:     ctx: Click context.     name: Feature group name.
